  "scope": "Candidate1559 extends accepted candidate1324 by 235 mathematical modules and 27,784 physical Lean lines, giving 1,559 modules and 258,073 lines. This checkpoint retains the four approved literal Stacks assumptions. The selected sources include the explicitly reviewed GraphCartierFactorization local-instance repair dc519c7f; its original maps and public claims are preserved.\n\nThe delta proves actual affine quasicoherent finite generation and section-extension/gluing results, the original projective coordinate line bundle's ampleness, positive degree on curves for ample restrictions and positive ample self-intersection, and positive-degree ampleness on the original projective line. It adds actual symmetric-algebra and affine projective-spectrum comparisons, with their precise finite-type, affine-base and empty-spectrum scope. These are separately proved adapters, not a general relative-Proj projectivity or arbitrary-stage blowup incidence producer.\n\nThe conormal and differential additions identify the original ideal quotients, duals, normal modules, K\u00e4hler pullbacks, exterior maps and tensor comparisons on their actual affine/open charts. The two original Frobenius Rees charts have their native determinant maps and exceptional-ideal tensor factorizations, including the whole-map comparisons with intrinsic differentials. The selected chart adjunction and equation-independence results retain their original smoothness, regular-equation and chart hypotheses. Full global adjunction descent, the later whole-stage canonical formula, Serre duality and Riemann-Roch are not concluded by these chart results.\n\nThe actual multicentre exceptional curves now have the computed intersection and ruling rows, original Picard realization and coordinate left inverse, and the retained seven-curve characteristic-two configuration with its actual Cartier parity statements. Original projectivity and field/centre hypotheses remain explicit where present. The seven curves are a constructed disjoint smooth rational minus-two family; the parity halves are Picard classes. These results do not assert a contraction, classification of all negative curves, or a singular-point bound.\n\nBigness results use the existing global-section-growth definition: zero-dimensional integral proper varieties over any field, positive-degree proper curves, the degree-zero converse under its stated integral/algebraically closed hypotheses, and actual prime-curve restrictions. Rational Hodge transport retains its explicit integral Hodge assumption. The four Hartshorne source-translation modules define full original propositions and retain raw statement premises in their conditional consumers; all five private Hartshorne axiom modules and their transitive consumers remain outside this checkpoint. No named manuscript theorem or supporting-obligation status is promoted by the module integration alone.",
